  "finalReply": "Done. All requirements are implemented and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Installed R** (`r-base-core` 4.3.3) and wrote the modular implementation to **`/app/ars.R`** (base R only, no extra packages), following Gilks & Wild (1992).\n\n**Primary function `ars(g, n, a, b, x0, max_proposals, concavity_tol, ...)`**\n- `g` is any vectorized (possibly unnormalized) density such as `dnorm`; extra distribution parameters pass through `...`; domain `[a, b]` supports `-Inf`/`Inf` ends.\n- Modular helpers, all snake_case functions: `validate_ars_inputs`, `probe_points`, `default_starting_points`, `eval_log_density`, `log_density_deriv` (central differences with step-halving fallback), `check_slope_order`, `build_envelope` (breakpoints, log-stable weights), `sample_envelope` (mixture of truncated exponentials via memoryless-property sampling — no overflow), `upper_hull`, `lower_hull`.\n- **Log-concavity checks at setup and after every evaluated proposal**: decreasing tangent slopes (scale-aware tolerance so flat/log-linear cases like exponential and uniform pass), tangent-intersection containment/ordering, and the defining check `h(x*) ≤ upper hull` — any violation stops with a \"not log-concave\" error.\n\n**Test function `test()`** — 12/12 passing, each printing `TEST_NAME: PASS/FAIL` with mean/sd statistics:\n- Overall sampler vs. known truth (mean/sd tolerances + KS tests): Normal(0,1), Exp(1), Gamma(2,1), Beta(2,5), Uniform(0,1), half-normal — confirming samples follow the target shape.\n- Module tests: numerical-derivative accuracy (max err 0) and envelope validity (upper hull bounds the log-density everywhere, zero violation).\n- Input validation: negative/zero/fractional `n`, `a ≥ b`, non-function `g`, non-vectorized density all rejected; non-log-concave Beta(0.5,0.5) reliably flagged.\n\n**Sample files generated**: `/app/normal_samples.txt` (5000 draws, mean −0.019, sd 0.996) and `/app/exponential_samples.txt` (5000 draws, mean 0.995, sd 0.997).",
